      "body": "## Motivation\n\n#43722 added `adjust_component_size` to both tree cores, but the two disagree when a delta would drive a ledger below zero:\n\n- Rust (`unified_tree_core.rs:adjust_component_size`) uses checked arithmetic and returns `InvalidComponentSizeDelta` (a `ValueError` in Python), leaving both ledgers untouched. Its own test `component_size_adjustment_errors_preserve_both_ledgers` pins that contract.\n- Python adds the delta unconditionally, so the same call silently records a negative evictable or protected size.\n\nNo production component calls the API yet, so nothing is wrong today. But Rust is the default core, so a component written and tested against one core would behave differently on the other the day it starts calling `adjust_component_size`.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `UnifiedTreeCore.adjust_component_size` (Python) raises `ValueError` before touching the ledger when `current + delta < 0`, with the same fields as the Rust error.\n- The interface docstring states the contract.\n\nPython ints cannot overflow, so only the underflow half of the Rust check applies.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New `test_underflowing_adjustment_raises_and_preserves_ledgers`, parametrized over both backends and over an evictable and a protected node. It checks that `-5` and `-(1 << 63)` raise and leave both ledgers unchanged, and that an exact `-4` still lands at zero.\n- Negative control: with the old Python core, both `python` cases fail (`DID NOT RAISE ValueError`) and both `rust` cases pass.\n- `test_rust_tree_core_integration.py`: 469 passed. `test_unified_radix_cache_unittest.py` and `test_rust_unified_radix_cache_unittest.py`: 2916 each, OK. The Rust extension was built from this tree.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38674268462](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38674268462)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38674268340](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38674268340)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38674268323](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38674268323)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
